-- Tests for bc-interpretation-commencement.l4 (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 3(4), 5(2), 16(1), 16(3), 20(1), 20(2), 20(5)).
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run. Every limb of a rule is tested on both
-- sides. A case the text does not answer is asserted as the named refusal with its message (NOTES.md, finding 2).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-commencement`


§ `s 3(4) The date of assent is part of the Act`
-- 3 (4): "The date of assent or signification is part of the Act."
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the date is part of the Act` `The date of assent`
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the date is part of the Act` `The date of signification`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3(4) the date is part of the Act` `Another date`
        BECAUSE "s 3(4) speaks only of the date of assent and the date of signification"

§ `s 5(2) Staggered commencement`
-- 5 (2): "If an enactment is to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council, (a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of any provision of the enactment"
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `In some other way` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
-- (b) "proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times for different provisions of the enactment."
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` `In some other way` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"

§ `s 16 Proclamation`
-- 16 (1): "In a proclamation, it is not necessary to mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) a proclamation must mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 16(1) a proclamation must mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 16(1) speaks only of a proclamation"
-- 16 (3): "If an enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation, judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation without being specially pleaded."
#ASSERT `s 16(3) judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(3) the issue of the proclamation must be specially pleaded` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 16(3) judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 16(3) the issue of the proclamation must be specially pleaded` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation"

§ `s 20 Appointments of officers`
-- 20 (1): "appointing instrument means an enactment that appoints a person to an office." "means" closes the definition: both limbs are needed.
#ASSERT `s 20(1) an instrument is an appointing instrument` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20(1) an instrument is an appointing instrument` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20(1) an instrument is an appointing instrument` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20(1) an instrument is an appointing instrument` FALSE FALSE)
-- 20 (2): "An authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint during pleasure."
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the authority to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint in this way` `During pleasure` TRUE
-- Fork F-pleasure: the sentence does not say the authority is only for appointment during pleasure (s 22(a) adds the power to set a term), so a fixed term is a refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20(2) the authority to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint in this way` `For a fixed term` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20(2) the authority to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint in this way` `In some other way` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20(2) the authority to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint in this way` `During pleasure` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 20(2) speaks only of an authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer"
-- Nor does it say what appointment during pleasure allows.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20(2) does not say what an appointment during pleasure allows: ending it at will, without notice or without cause`
        BECAUSE "s 20(2) does not say what an appointment during pleasure allows: ending it at will, without notice or without cause"
-- 20 (5): "Section 4 [time of commencement or repeal] does not apply to an appointing instrument or an enactment referred to in subsection (4) (c), (d) or (e)."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20(5) section 4 applies to the instrument or enactment` `An appointing instrument`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20(5) section 4 applies to the instrument or enactment` `An enactment referred to in section 20(4)(c), (d) or (e)`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20(5) section 4 applies to the instrument or enactment` `Another enactment`
        BECAUSE "s 20(5) says where section 4 does not apply and does not say it applies everywhere else"

